{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r1s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Fetch-stage direct-branch prediction with a small history table\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current core resolves every taken branch and JAL in EX, then discards\n  the younger instruction being fetched in that cycle. CoreMark repeatedly\n  executes loop and decision branches, so this branch bubble recurs throughout\n  the timed region. The measured critical path is through the M-extension ALU,\n  leaving room for a compact predictor without targeting that path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Predict direct control flow in IF: JAL is always taken, and a 128-entry\n  two-bit saturating branch history table predicts conditional branches.\n  Untrained entries use backward-taken/forward-not-taken as the cold-start\n  direction. Form the B/J immediate and predicted next PC from the fetched\n  instruction; advance the PC to that address only when the instruction bus\n  is ready and the existing pipeline stall rules allow it. Carry the predicted\n  next PC with the instruction through ID/EX. Never predict a misaligned\n  direct target, which will trap in EX. In EX, compare the prediction with the\n  resolved next PC and redirect/flush only on a mismatch, including a\n  misaligned-target trap; train the table once when a valid branch advances\n  from EX. Keep JALR on the existing resolve path. This should remove the\n  normal one-cycle penalty for taken JALs and correctly predicted branches\n  while preserving the exact retirement and RVFI behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Decode direct branch/JAL targets during fetch, consult and train a small two-bit direction table, and select the predicted PC under existing stalls.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Carry the fetch prediction into ID/EX without altering decode or retirement.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare predicted and actual next PC, redirect only on a valid misprediction, and expose one branch-training event per advancing branch.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect branch prediction metadata and EX training to IF, and gate correction during a held EX stage.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Flush the younger instructions only on an EX misprediction while retaining load-use and bus-stall priority.\"\n  - file: test/test_predictor.py\n    description: \"Check taken and untaken branches, JAL, cold-start direction, misprediction recovery, and stalls without changing the existing invariant checks.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
