{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short; sed -n '1,100p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-001-r1s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-001-r1s0\ntitle: \"Replace combinational division with a radix-4 iterative unit\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The baseline's 199.837 ns worst path passes through the EX ALU, whose\n  combinational 32-bit divide and remainder operators dominate logic depth.\n  That sets Fmax to 5.442 MHz even when CoreMark executes no divide in a\n  given cycle. A compact iterative divider trades latency on rare divide\n  instructions for a much shorter clock period on every instruction.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace all DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU combinational operators with one\n  shared radix-4 unsigned restoring divider that resolves two quotient bits\n  per cycle, at most 16 iterations. Convert signed operands to magnitudes\n  on launch and correct quotient/remainder signs on completion. Handle\n  divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 exactly as RV32M specifies. Interlock EX\n  while the divider runs: hold IF and ID/EX, let older instructions drain,\n  insert bubbles into EX/MEM, and emit the division result exactly once\n  when ready. Preserve the ALTOPS stand-ins in formal mode. The real-mode\n  interval from the previous retirement through a division retirement\n  must remain within the existing 20-cycle liveness bound. The expected\n  Fmax improvement should outweigh the extra CoreMark divide cycles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 50\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove the real-mode combinational divide and remainder data paths while preserving the exact ALTOPS expressions and all other ALU operations.\"\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: \"Add a shared radix-4 sequential quotient/remainder unit with signed pre/post processing, RV32M corner cases, and a one-result handshake.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Launch division with forwarded operands, select its result for EX/MEM, and inject EX/MEM bubbles while it runs without repeating side effects or losing forwarding data.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect divider busy/done state to the pipeline interlock and preserve the existing single-channel RVFI port and retirement order.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Coordinate divide holds with load-use, imem backpressure, dmem backpressure, and redirect priority while allowing older instructions to drain.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Exercise the sequential divider handshake and exact results of all eight RV32M operations, including signs, zero divisors, and overflow.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
