{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r1s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-002-r1s1\ntitle: \"Move division off the single-cycle execute path\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The baseline reaches only 5.442 MHz, and its 156-cell critical path runs\n  from MEM/WB forwarding through EX arithmetic toward the data-memory port.\n  The combinational RV32M quotient and remainder operators force a full\n  32-bit divide network into this one-cycle EX path, while also contributing\n  substantial logic to the 12,312-LUT design. CoreMark should benefit more\n  from a shorter common EX path than it loses to the latency of infrequent\n  DIV and REM instructions.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the synthesized combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath in the\n  production core with one shared, iterative radix-2 divider. Keep the\n  instruction in EX while the divider runs; let older MEM and WB operations\n  drain, inject bubbles into EX/MEM, and retire the divide exactly once when\n  its registered result is ready. Handle signed quotient/remainder correction,\n  divide by zero, and INT_MIN / -1 explicitly. Preserve the combinational\n  ALU unit-test interface and the existing RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS behavior, but\n  ensure the timed core does not instantiate an active combinational divide\n  path. This should substantially raise Fmax and reduce LUT use at a modest\n  CoreMark cycle cost.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 25\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: \"Add a shared 32-round unsigned restoring divider with signed operand/result correction and exact RV32M corner cases.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Start and track DIV/REM in EX, select the registered iterative result, and issue each completed operation to EX/MEM only once.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect divide-busy and divide-complete control to pipeline stalls and bubbles while allowing older memory operations to drain.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add divide interlock priority relative to load-use, bus stalls, and redirects without dropping or duplicating instructions.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Keep direct ALU arithmetic tests and ALTOPS semantics intact while isolating combinational division from the synthesized production execute path.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
