{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\"|structural|hyp-20260929-002-r1s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move division off the single-cycle execute path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline reaches only 5.442 MHz, and its 156-cell critical path runs\\nfrom MEM/WB forwarding through EX arithmetic toward the data-memory port.\\nThe combinational RV32M quotient and remainder operators force a full\\n32-bit divide network into this one-cycle EX path, while also contributing\\nsubstantial logic to the 12,312-LUT design. CoreMark should benefit more\\nfrom a shorter common EX path than it loses to the latency of infrequent\\nDIV and REM instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline reaches only 5.442 MHz, and its 156-cell critical path runs\\nfrom MEM/WB forwarding through EX arithmetic toward the data-memory port.\\nThe combinational RV32M quotient and remainder operators force a full\\n32-bit divide network into this one-cycle EX path, while also contributing\\nsubstantial logic to the 12,312-LUT design. CoreMark should benefit more\\nfrom a shorter common EX path than it loses to the latency of infrequent\\nDIV and REM instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the synthesized combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath in the\\nproduction core with one shared, 16-step radix-4 restoring divider. Keep the\\ninstruction in EX while the divider runs; let older MEM and WB operations\\ndrain, inject bubbles into EX/MEM, and retire the divide exactly once when\\nits registered result is ready. Handle signed quotient/remainder correction,\\ndivide by zero, and INT_MIN / -1 explicitly. Preserve the combinational\\nALU unit-test interface and the existing RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS behavior via\\na constant ALU parameter: direct ALU tests use combinational division,\\nwhile the core disables it and takes divide results from the iterative\\nunit. Complete division and retirement within the formal suite's 20-cycle\\nliveness window. This should substantially raise Fmax and reduce LUT use\\nat a modest CoreMark cycle cost.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 25, \"confidence\": \"me\n…[1574 of 4646 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6ce05f04a1e5203e]…\n bus stalls, and redirects without dropping or duplicating instructions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Parameterize combinational DIV/REM so standalone ALU tests retain it, while the production core constant-disables it; preserve ALTOPS formulas.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 101.08, \"delta_pct\": 733.99, \"vs_baseline\": 733.99, \"fmax_mhz\": 45.399, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2830, \"ff\": 662, \"seeds\": [46.017, 45.399, 45.399], \"perturbations\": [[0, 46.017, 21], [1, 45.399, 20], [2, 45.399, 20]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs1_val_0_s100\", \"slack_ns\": -16.731, \"arrival_ns\": 27.025, \"logic_cells\": 44, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_hazard\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 21, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T18:15:51.001126Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 1}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
