{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r2s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-002-r2s1\ntitle: \"Resolve redirects from the registered EX/MEM stage\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The iterative divider removed the 200 ns arithmetic path, but the current\n  champion's 27.889 ns worst path still runs through EX branch resolution,\n  IF PC selection, hazard control, and the ID/EX register enable. A branch\n  decision computed from forwarded operands therefore reaches across three\n  pipeline stages in one cycle. Breaking this feedback path can raise Fmax\n  enough to outweigh one additional cycle on taken branches and jumps.\nhypothesis: |\n  Carry the resolved next PC and taken-control-transfer indication through\n  the existing EX/MEM register, then redirect IF from that registered state.\n  On the redirect cycle, squash the younger instruction in EX before it can\n  enter EX/MEM, flush ID, and set the fetch PC to the target. Gate divider\n  launch and all younger side effects on this squash. Issue each redirect\n  only while the valid branch or jump occupies MEM, with correct priority\n  against bus stalls and the existing divide interlock. Preserve misaligned\n  target traps, sequential RVFI retirement, and all load/store handshakes.\n  This moves branch comparison and target arithmetic out of the immediate\n  PC and ID flush path, aiming for a shorter clock with modest CPI cost.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 12\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Derive redirect and target from the registered EX/MEM control transfer, and connect a younger-EX squash signal.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Retain branch outcome and resolved next PC in EX/MEM, suppress EX/MEM capture and divider launch when an older MEM redirect squashes EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Prioritize registered redirects over front-end stalls and flush both younger pipeline stages without losing a pending memory operation.\"\n  - file: test/test_registered_redirect.py\n    description: \"Exercise taken branch and jump recovery with instruction stalls, data stalls, and a squashed younger divider.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
