{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_24", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 8 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-8fac2ef\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 12.12, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.442, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12312, \"ff\": 460, \"seeds\": [5.14, 5.442, 5.442], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.14, 150], [1, 5.442, 149], [2, 5.442, 149]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -189.542, \"arrival_ns\": 199.837, \"logic_cells\": 156, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 150, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T18:03:45.068034Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Replace combinational division with a radix-4 iterative unit\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline's 199.837 ns worst path passes through the EX ALU, whose\\ncombinational 32-bit divide and remainder operators dominate logic depth.\\nThat sets Fmax to 5.442 MHz even when CoreMark executes no divide in a\\ngiven cycle. A compact iterative divider trades latency on rare divide\\ninstructions for a much shorter clock period on every instruction.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline's 199.837 ns worst path passes through the EX ALU, whose\\ncombinational 32-bit divide and remainder operators dominate logic depth.\\nThat sets Fmax to 5.442 MHz even when CoreMark executes no divide in a\\ngiven cycle. A compact iterative divider trades latency on rare divide\\ninstructions for a much shorter clock period on every instruction.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace all DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU combinational operators with one\\nshared radix-4 unsigned restoring divider that resolves two quotient bits\\nper cycle, at most 16 iterations. Convert signed operands to magnitudes\\non launch and correct quotient/remainder signs on completion. Handle\\ndivide-by-zero\n…[12828 of 15900 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e50f8c0f5052744a]…\nng invariant checks.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 12.79, \"delta_pct\": 5.53, \"vs_baseline\": 5.53, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.373, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4202272, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 13018, \"ff\": 767, \"seeds\": [5.136, 5.373, 5.373], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.136, 147], [1, 5.373, 152], [2, 5.373, 152]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_2_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -189.718, \"arrival_ns\": 200.012, \"logic_cells\": 156, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_rf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 147, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T18:25:45.087943Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-003-r1s2 (regression, +5.53%): A 128-entry IF branch history table yields only a modest CoreMark gain while the combinational RV32M EX path still limits clock speed, so branch-bubble savings cannot match shortening that path.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
